IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VII, sections 70 to 75 -- DELIVERY AND
-- OWNERSHIP THROUGH A BROKER; RECLAIMING A SECURITY; THE RIGHT TO REQUISITES FOR REGISTRATION; SEIZURE;
-- AGENTS WHO ACT IN GOOD FAITH. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on another section's rule calls it and takes its inputs. Across
-- modules a plain input stands in for the other rule's result, and the comment names the rule that works it
-- out (here: s 72(2) takes the result of s 68(1), which is in cb2-part7-endorsement.l4).

§ `s 70 Constructive delivery of a security`

§§ `s 70(1) Constructive delivery of a security`

-- Paragraphs (b) and (c) are the two ways delivery occurs through the purchaser's broker; s 70(2) singles
-- them out, so they have a rule of their own.
-- src:982 | 70 (1) Delivery to a purchaser occurs when
-- src:983 | (a) the purchaser or a person designated by the purchaser acquires possession of a security;
-- src:984 | (b) the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser;
-- src:985 | (c) the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser; or
-- src:986 | (d) with respect to an identified security to be delivered while still in the possession of a third person, that person acknowledges holding it for the purchaser.
@ref CBCA s 70(1) (src:982-986)
GIVEN `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`delivery occurs through the purchaser's broker within s 70(1)` MEANS
        `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser`
    OR  `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser`

-- src:982 | 70 (1) Delivery to a purchaser occurs when
-- src:983 | (a) the purchaser or a person designated by the purchaser acquires possession of a security;
-- src:984 | (b) the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser;
-- src:985 | (c) the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser; or
-- src:986 | (d) with respect to an identified security to be delivered while still in the possession of a third person, that person acknowledges holding it for the purchaser.
@ref CBCA s 70(1) (src:982-986)
GIVEN `the purchaser or a person designated by the purchaser acquires possession of a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a third person in possession of an identified security to be delivered acknowledges holding it for the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`delivery to a purchaser occurs within s 70(1)` MEANS
        `the purchaser or a person designated by the purchaser acquires possession of a security`
    OR  `delivery occurs through the purchaser's broker within s 70(1)`
            `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser`
            `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser`
    OR  `a third person in possession of an identified security to be delivered acknowledges holding it for the purchaser`

§§ `s 70(2) Constructive ownership`

-- src:987 | Constructive ownership
-- src:988 | (2) A purchaser is the owner of a security that a broker holds for the purchaser, but is not a holder except in the cases referred to in paragraphs (1)(b) and (c).
@ref CBCA s 70(2) (src:987-988)
GIVEN `a broker holds the security for the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchaser is the owner of a security that a broker holds for the purchaser within s 70(2)` MEANS
    `a broker holds the security for the purchaser`

-- src:987 | Constructive ownership
-- src:988 | (2) A purchaser is the owner of a security that a broker holds for the purchaser, but is not a holder except in the cases referred to in paragraphs (1)(b) and (c).
@ref CBCA s 70(2) (src:987-988)
GIVEN `a broker holds the security for the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchaser is a holder of a security that a broker holds for the purchaser within s 70(2)` MEANS
        `a broker holds the security for the purchaser`
    AND `delivery occurs through the purchaser's broker within s 70(1)`
            `the broker of the purchaser acquires possession of a security specially endorsed to or issued in the name of the purchaser`
            `the broker of the purchaser sends the purchaser confirmation of the purchase and identifies in a record a specific security as belonging to the purchaser`

§§ `s 70(3) Ownership of part of fungible bulk`

-- The purchaser owns a proportionate share of the bulk: the number purchased over the number in the bulk.
-- NOTHING: the security is not part of a fungible bulk, or the bulk is empty.
-- src:989 | Ownership of part of fungible bulk
-- src:990 | (3) If a security is part of a fungible bulk, a purchaser of the security is the owner of a proportionate share in the fungible bulk.
@ref CBCA s 70(3) (src:989-990)
GIVEN `the security is part of a fungible bulk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of securities the purchaser purchased` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of securities in the fungible bulk` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the purchaser's proportionate share of the fungible bulk within s 70(3)` MEANS
    IF     `the security is part of a fungible bulk`
       AND `the number of securities in the fungible bulk` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the number of securities the purchaser purchased` DIVIDED BY `the number of securities in the fungible bulk`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 70(4) Notice to broker`

-- src:991 | Notice to broker
-- src:992 | (4) Notice of an adverse claim received by a broker or by a purchaser after the broker takes delivery as a holder for value is not effective against the broker or the purchaser, except that, as between the broker and the purchaser, the purchaser may demand delivery of an equivalent security as to which no notice of an adverse claim has been received.
@ref CBCA s 70(4) (src:991-992)
GIVEN `the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of an adverse claim is ineffective against the broker and the purchaser within s 70(4)` MEANS
    `the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value`

-- Between the broker and the purchaser, the purchaser may demand delivery of an equivalent security as to
-- which no notice of an adverse claim has been received.
-- src:991 | Notice to broker
-- src:992 | (4) Notice of an adverse claim received by a broker or by a purchaser after the broker takes delivery as a holder for value is not effective against the broker or the purchaser, except that, as between the broker and the purchaser, the purchaser may demand delivery of an equivalent security as to which no notice of an adverse claim has been received.
@ref CBCA s 70(4) (src:991-992)
GIVEN `the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchaser may demand delivery of an equivalent security from the broker within s 70(4)` MEANS
    `the notice was received by the broker, or by the purchaser after the broker took delivery as a holder for value`

§ `s 71 Delivery of security`

§§ `s 71(1) Delivery of security`

-- "Unless otherwise agreed", where a sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers.
-- src:994 | 71 (1) Unless otherwise agreed, if a sale of a security is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers,
-- src:995 | (a) the selling customer fulfils their duty to deliver by delivering the security to the selling broker or to a person designated by the selling broker or by causing an acknowledgment to be made to the selling broker that it is held for the selling broker; and
-- src:996 | (b) the selling broker, including a correspondent broker, acting for a selling customer fulfils their duty to deliver by delivering the security or a like security to the buying broker or to a person designated by the buying broker or by effecting clearance of the sale in accordance with the rules of the exchange on which the transaction took place.
@ref CBCA s 71(1)(a) (src:994-995)
GIVEN `the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the selling customer delivers the security to the selling broker or to a person designated by the selling broker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the selling customer causes an acknowledgment to be made to the selling broker that the security is held for the selling broker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the selling customer has fulfilled the duty to deliver within s 71(1)` MEANS
        `the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers`
    AND (NOT `the parties otherwise agreed`)
    AND (   `the selling customer delivers the security to the selling broker or to a person designated by the selling broker`
         OR `the selling customer causes an acknowledgment to be made to the selling broker that the security is held for the selling broker`)

-- src:994 | 71 (1) Unless otherwise agreed, if a sale of a security is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers,
-- src:995 | (a) the selling customer fulfils their duty to deliver by delivering the security to the selling broker or to a person designated by the selling broker or by causing an acknowledgment to be made to the selling broker that it is held for the selling broker; and
-- src:996 | (b) the selling broker, including a correspondent broker, acting for a selling customer fulfils their duty to deliver by delivering the security or a like security to the buying broker or to a person designated by the buying broker or by effecting clearance of the sale in accordance with the rules of the exchange on which the transaction took place.
@ref CBCA s 71(1)(b) (src:994-996)
GIVEN `the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the selling broker delivers the security or a like security to the buying broker or to a person designated by the buying broker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the selling broker effects clearance of the sale in accordance with the rules of the exchange on which the transaction took place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the selling broker has fulfilled the duty to deliver within s 71(1)` MEANS
        `the sale is made on an exchange or otherwise through brokers`
    AND (NOT `the parties otherwise agreed`)
    AND (   `the selling broker delivers the security or a like security to the buying broker or to a person designated by the buying broker`
         OR `the selling broker effects clearance of the sale in accordance with the rules of the exchange on which the transaction took place`)

§§ `s 71(2) Duty to deliver`

-- src:997 | Duty to deliver
-- src:998 | (2) Subject to this section and unless otherwise agreed, a transferor’s duty to deliver a security under a contract of purchase is not fulfilled until the transferor delivers the security in negotiable form to the purchaser or to a person designated by the purchaser, or causes an acknowledgment to be made to the purchaser that the security is held for the purchaser.
@ref CBCA s 71(2) (src:997-998)
GIVEN `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor delivers the security in negotiable form to the purchaser or to a person designated by the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor causes an acknowledgment to be made to the purchaser that the security is held for the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the transferor has fulfilled the duty to deliver under a contract of purchase within s 71(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the parties otherwise agreed`)
    AND (   `the transferor delivers the security in negotiable form to the purchaser or to a person designated by the purchaser`
         OR `the transferor causes an acknowledgment to be made to the purchaser that the security is held for the purchaser`)

§§ `s 71(3) Delivery to broker`

-- src:999 | Delivery to broker
-- src:1000 | (3) A sale to a broker purchasing for the broker’s own account is subject to subsection (2) and not subsection (1), unless the sale is made on a stock exchange.
@ref CBCA s 71(3) (src:999-1000)
GIVEN `the sale is to a broker purchasing for the broker's own account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is made on a stock exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsection 71(2) governs the sale and subsection 71(1) does not within s 71(3)` MEANS
        `the sale is to a broker purchasing for the broker's own account`
    AND (NOT `the sale is made on a stock exchange`)

§ `s 72 Right to reclaim possession`

§§ `s 72(1) Right to reclaim possession`

-- src:1001 | Right to reclaim possession
-- src:1002 | 72 (1) A person against whom the transfer of a security is wrongful for any reason, including incapacity, may against anyone except a bona fide purchaser reclaim possession of the security or obtain possession of any new security evidencing all or part of the same rights or claim damages.
@ref CBCA s 72(1) (src:1001-1002)
GIVEN `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may reclaim possession, obtain a new security or claim damages within s 72(1)` MEANS
        `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity`
    AND (NOT `the other party is a bona fide purchaser`)

§§ `s 72(2) Recovery if unauthorized endorsement`

-- The second input is the result of `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the endorsement against
-- the other party within s 68(1)` (cb2-part7-endorsement.l4), for the same purchaser.
-- src:1003 | Recovery if unauthorized endorsement
-- src:1004 | (2) If the transfer of a security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement, the owner may reclaim possession of the security or a new security even from a bona fide purchaser if the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement may be asserted against such purchaser under section 68.
@ref CBCA s 72(2) (src:1003-1004)
GIVEN `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the owner may reclaim possession even from a bona fide purchaser within s 72(2)` MEANS
        `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement`
    AND `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68`

-- The right to reclaim possession arises under (1) or (2).
-- src:1001 | Right to reclaim possession
-- src:1002 | 72 (1) A person against whom the transfer of a security is wrongful for any reason, including incapacity, may against anyone except a bona fide purchaser reclaim possession of the security or obtain possession of any new security evidencing all or part of the same rights or claim damages.
-- src:1003 | Recovery if unauthorized endorsement
-- src:1004 | (2) If the transfer of a security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement, the owner may reclaim possession of the security or a new security even from a bona fide purchaser if the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement may be asserted against such purchaser under section 68.
@ref CBCA s 72(1)-(2) (src:1001-1004)
GIVEN `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person has a right to reclaim possession of the security within s 72(2)` MEANS
        `the person may reclaim possession, obtain a new security or claim damages within s 72(1)`
            `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity`
            `the other party is a bona fide purchaser`
    OR  `the owner may reclaim possession even from a bona fide purchaser within s 72(2)`
            `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement`
            `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68`

§§ `s 72(3) Remedies`

-- src:1005 | Remedies
-- src:1006 | (3) The right to reclaim possession of a security may be specifically enforced, its transfer may be restrained and the security may be impounded or, in Quebec, sequestrated pending litigation.
@ref CBCA s 72(3) (src:1005-1006)
GIVEN `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party is a bona fide purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the right to reclaim possession may be specifically enforced, the transfer restrained and the security impounded or sequestrated pending litigation within s 72(3)` MEANS
    `the person has a right to reclaim possession of the security within s 72(2)`
        `the transfer of the security is wrongful against the person for any reason, including incapacity`
        `the other party is a bona fide purchaser`
        `the transfer of the security is wrongful by reason of an unauthorized endorsement`
        `the owner may assert the ineffectiveness of the purported endorsement against the purchaser under section 68`

§ `s 73 Right to requisites for registration`

§§ `s 73(1) Right to requisites for registration`

-- "Unless otherwise agreed", on demand; but if the transfer is not for value the transferor need not
-- supply them unless the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer.
-- src:1007 | Right to requisites for registration
-- src:1008 | 73 (1) Unless otherwise agreed, a transferor shall on demand supply a purchaser with proof of authority to transfer or with any other requisite that is necessary to obtain registration of the transfer of a security, but if the transfer is not for value a transferor need not do so unless the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer.
@ref CBCA s 73(1) (src:1007-1008)
GIVEN `the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is for value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the transferor must supply the proof or requisite within s 73(1)` MEANS
        `the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer`
    AND (NOT `the parties otherwise agreed`)
    AND (   `the transfer is for value`
         OR `the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer`)

§§ `s 73(2) Rescission of transfer`

-- src:1009 | Rescission of transfer
-- src:1010 | (2) If the transferor fails to comply with a demand under subsection (1) within a reasonable time, the purchaser may reject or rescind the transfer.
@ref CBCA s 73(2) (src:1009-1010)
GIVEN `the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is for value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor fails to comply with the demand within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchaser may reject or rescind the transfer within s 73(2)` MEANS
        `the transferor must supply the proof or requisite within s 73(1)`
            `the purchaser demands proof of authority to transfer or another requisite necessary to obtain registration of the transfer`
            `the parties otherwise agreed`
            `the transfer is for value`
            `the purchaser pays the reasonable and necessary costs of the proof and transfer`
    AND `the transferor fails to comply with the demand within a reasonable time`

§ `s 74 Seizure of security`

-- src:1011 | Seizure of security
-- src:1012 | 74 No seizure of a security or other interest or right evidenced by the security is effective until the person making the seizure obtains possession of the security.
@ref CBCA s 74 (src:1011-1012)
GIVEN `the person making the seizure obtains possession of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the seizure is ineffective within s 74` MEANS
    NOT `the person making the seizure obtains possession of the security`

§ `s 75 No liability for acts in good faith`

-- "In good faith, including observance of reasonable commercial standards if the agent or mandatary or the
-- bailee is in the business of buying, selling or otherwise dealing with securities of a corporation".
-- That the principal has no right to dispose of the securities makes no difference, so no input asks.
-- src:1013 | No liability for acts in good faith
-- src:1014 | 75 An agent or mandatary or a bailee who in good faith, including observance of reasonable commercial standards if the agent or mandatary or the bailee is in the business of buying, selling or otherwise dealing with securities of a corporation has received securities and sold, pledged or delivered them, according to the instructions of their principal or mandator, is not liable for conversion or for participation in breach of fiduciary duty although the principal has no right to dispose of them.
@ref CBCA s 75 (src:1013-1014)
GIVEN `the person is an agent, mandatary or bailee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has received securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person sold, pledged or delivered them according to the instructions of their principal or mandator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in the business of buying, selling or otherwise dealing with securities of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person observed reasonable commercial standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is not liable for conversion or for participation in breach of fiduciary duty within s 75` MEANS
        `the person is an agent, mandatary or bailee`
    AND `the person has received securities`
    AND `the person sold, pledged or delivered them according to the instructions of their principal or mandator`
    AND `the person acted in good faith`
    AND (   (NOT `the person is in the business of buying, selling or otherwise dealing with securities of a corporation`)
         OR `the person observed reasonable commercial standards`)
